<title>USA: U.S. cigarette makers to buy 473.5 mln lbs tobacco.</title>
<headline>U.S. cigarette makers to buy 473.5 mln lbs tobacco.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Wednesday said the nation's cigarette manufacturers plan to buy 473.5 milion pounds (farm sales weight) of 1997 crop burley tobacco.</p>
<p>The U.S. tobacco industry by law must report to the department annually their intended purchases of burley tobacco from domestic auction markets and producers.</p>
<p>In 1996, intended purchases totaled 424 million pounds.</p>
</text>
